            <div xml:id="d688">

                <pb facs="0944" n="830" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg830"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.754/13</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Albania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Holmes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tirana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-13">March 13, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received March
                        28.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 765</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction No. 254 of October 23, 1929, directing that a treaty of
                    naturalization be proposed to the Albanian Government, and that pending the
                    signature of such treaty an informal agreement be entered into providing that
                    persons born in the United States of Albanian parents, while maintaining their
                    residence in the United States, will be allowed to visit Albania, temporarily,
                    without being held liable for military or other national service.</p>
                <p>There is transmitted herewith five copies of a translation of a note giving such
                    assurance received from the Albanian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julius C. Holmes</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d688-a1.xml" xpointer="d688-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
